The rain is suddenly very heavy.
I run quickly to a small museum by the park.
Museums are fortunately always open on Sundays.
I wipe the water from my face and go to the ticket desk.
The man at the ticket desk greets me warmly.
"One ticket, please," I say.
"That is six euros," he says.
I pay and he gives me the ticket and the till receipt.
"You need this till receipt later," the man explains.
"And the backpack must go into the cloakroom."
"Do I have to hand in this wet jacket too?" I ask.
"No, you can keep the jacket on," he answers.
I go to the cloakroom and hand over the backpack.
Then I go into the empty exhibition halls.
Ten minutes ago I was still outside in the rain.
But in here it is wonderfully dry and quiet.
